// Chase fixtures for the revision-event-6 strata: the event-rate
// envelope lane, the distance judgments, the timed core, the
// discharge kit, and the grounded-walk seam — in theory vocabulary
// (transposed relations keep function names; unary attributes take
// the synthesized `arg` field; ground fields ride abstract
// elements). Instance blocks in one file chase jointly in one model,
// so element names are unique across the file. The battery greps the
// chase transcript for named derived rows and judgments — never exit
// codes alone.
//
// Walk loci (kit coverage, arithmetic ties, oracle content) are
// loud-defer-never-silent-green until the provider realizations
// land: at this tier the instrument is the DEMAND ROW — it must
// mint per entity, and its minting axiom's demotion must be a named
// RED. The refuse/report tier (constructor disjointness, range
// reports) lives at the theory surface, census-fenced.

// The event-rate consumes traversal, both faces and both depths: a
// spec consuming SRateLE directly, and a disjunction spec whose
// RIGHT arm consumes SRateGE — the roster projection must reach the
// roster through the or-walk (the traversal-growth check: rosters
// inside SRate* formers are reached by spec_consumes_trs, the
// spec_consumes_ret analog), and the roster-conformance demand must
// mint at each pairing. The left arm consumes an opaque component:
// the absence half asserts the projection does not leak onto
// non-rate components, and the cross-pairing absence half asserts
// demands key to their own pairing.
instance E6RateConsumes : Qtsl {
  rq, rq2 : QSat;
  rsy, rsy2 : System;
  rsd, rsl, rsr, rse : Spec;
  rfo, rfg, rfe : ForallSpec;
  rst1, rst2 : TrList;
  rrho, rsig : Q;

  // direct LE consumer, paired with rsy2
  [arg: rq2, out: rsy2] QSat/sys;
  [arg: rq2, out: rse] QSat/spec;
  [rho: rrho, sigma: rsig, trs: rst1, out: rfe] SRateLE;
  [spec: rse, f: rfe] spec_forall;

  // GE consumer one disjunction deep, paired with rsy
  [arg: rq, out: rsy] QSat/sys;
  [arg: rq, out: rsd] QSat/spec;
  [spec: rsd, left: rsl, right: rsr] spec_or;
  [spec: rsl, f: rfo] spec_forall;
  [rho: rrho, sigma: rsig, trs: rst2, out: rfg] SRateGE;
  [spec: rsr, f: rfg] spec_forall;
}

// The event-rate certificate lane's three node species: premise-free
// per-entity walk demands (the QDeadlineTable pattern). The kit
// content (interior/guard-counted rows, wing prices, the instant
// member's cbAdditive budget citation) is walk material at the
// ground seam — an unrealized walk defers loudly on these rows,
// never accepts.
instance E6RateNodes : Qtsl {
  rub : QRateUB;
  rlb : QRateLB;
  rfc : QRateFromClocks;
}

// The distance-functor registry (all three v0 entries symmetric —
// the derived marker the judgment-level admissibles will consume)
// and the three distance-concluding node species. qdW1's entity is
// registry-legal; concluding THROUGH it is the walk-fenced entry
// license (D-3, walk-side), not a formation fact.
instance E6DistRegistry : Qtsl {
  qdt, qdw, qdg : QDistEntry;
  qdr : PathObservable;

  [out: qdt] qdTV;
  [out: qdw] qdW1;
  [ret: qdr, out: qdg] qdGap;
}

instance E6DistNodes : Qtsl {
  cdn : QCoupleDrift;
  fbn : QFixBall;
  dtn : QDistTransport;
}

// The timed core's three schema nodes: conclusion resolution
// (recompute lhs/rhs from node fields, class/rel fixed by schema)
// is each walk's whole content — loud-defer at this tier.
instance E6TimedNodes : Qtsl {
  tin : QInvRelativize;
  tfn : QFirstService;
  tsn : QFirstServiceSplit;
}

// The discharge kit's cover node: all four warrant-hypothesis
// carriers must mint as chased demands per entity — the split
// (hdecomp), the two cell-membership form obligations (the roster
// formula fields, cover and off), and the scope bridge (hbridge —
// the review round-1 exploit locus: an earlier spelling assigned the bridge
// to the consuming walk, leaving the conclusion pre unconstrained;
// the demand row below IS the repair, and its absence is the
// exploit's signature). The absence half asserts the scope formula
// takes the BRIDGE demand, never a cell-membership demand.
instance E6CoverKit : Qtsl {
  pvc : PVerifiedCover;
  vcx : QGridCx;
  vdm : Box;
  vff, vof, vcf, vsf : Formula;
  vk, vj, vnc, vno : Nat;

  [arg: pvc, out: vcx] PVerifiedCover/cx;
  [arg: pvc, out: vdm] PVerifiedCover/dom;
  [arg: pvc, out: vff] PVerifiedCover/off;
  [arg: pvc, out: vsf] PVerifiedCover/scopeF;
  [p: pvc, k: vk, out: vcf] PVerifiedCover/coverForm;
  [p: pvc, j: vj, out: vof] PVerifiedCover/offForm;

  // the indexed cell-membership demands ride the enumeration guard
  // (k < nCover, j < nOff): the guard rows are producer CLAIMS at
  // the ground seam (locked vocabulary — seedable, never decidable
  // by the chase), and with them claimed the two form obligations
  // must mint per indexed cell.
  [arg: pvc, out: vnc] PVerifiedCover/nCover;
  [arg: pvc, out: vno] PVerifiedCover/nOff;
  [l: vk, r: vnc] nat_lt;
  [l: vj, r: vno] nat_lt;
}

// The grounded-walk seam (the credal stratum's loud-defer face): a
// compiled verdict form mints the claim-keyed subject-side
// obligation bundle — where the sigma-face properness read, the
// per-entry containments, and the witness obligations live once the
// witness kits land. The sigma/zeta separating subject (all laws at
// positive finite penalty) is value-tier cargo for that walk; until
// it lands, the demand row's undischarged presence is the
// never-silent-green instrument. The spec-side recompute demand
// (exactly-one-SProper among the exists-face entries) mints beside
// it through the verdict_compile route.
instance E6GroundedForm : Qtsl {
  gfq : QSat;
  gfs : Spec;
  gfv : QVerdictForm;
  gib : QInitBridge;

  [arg: gfq, out: gfs] QSat/spec;
  [sat: gfq, form: gfv] qsat_verdict;
}
